ure for the latter case. ... Finally, we study the question of when a one-loop integral satisfies the Cohen-Macaulay property and show that for almost all choices of kinematics the Cohen-Macaulay property holds. ... In order to compute this discriminant, we present approaches from classical elimination theory, as well as a numerical algorithm based on homotopy continuation.\n\n# Principal Matroid Determinants\n\n  * April 2026\n\nDOI:10.48550/arXiv.2604.24667\n\nAuthors:\n\nSaiei-Jaeyeong Matsubara-Heo\n\nSaiei-Jaeyeong Matsubara-Heo\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nSimon Telen\n\n  * Max Planck Institute for Mathematics in the Sciences\n\n\n## Abstract\n\nWe develop a theory of principal determinants and hypergeometric systems for realizable matroids. Our framework parallels the toric theory of Gel'fand, Kapranov, and Zelevinsky (GKZ), but with the combinatorics of matroids and their flats replacing the usual role of polytopes and their faces. In this analogy, the toric variety is replaced by a reciprocal linear space. The {principal A-determinant} is replaced by the {principal matroid determinant}, defined as a specialization of a resultant. The GKZ hypergeometric system is replaced by the {matroid hypergeometric system}, a holonomic D-module of combinatorial nature whose singular locus is conjectured to be the principal matroid~determinant.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSimon Telen: Principal Matroid Determinants - Mittag-Leffler (https://www.mittag-leffler.se/seminar/simon-telen-reciprocal-a-determinants/)\nciteturn4search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; We develop a theory of principal determinants and hypergeometric systems for realizable matroids. ... Joint work with Saiei-Jaeyeong Matsubara-Heo, https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.24667.\n\n# Simon Telen: Principal Matroid Determinants\n\nDate: 2026-06-25\n\nTime: 09:00 - 09:45\n\nSpeaker\nSimon Telen, MPI Mi